  "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
  "instance_name": "award_to_terrorist",
  "label": "Award to Terrorist",
  "description": "The meme references a real-world event where the Canadian government awarded a $10.5 million compensation package to the family of a terrorist who killed a Canadian soldier in 2014. This event is the factual basis for the accusation in the meme. The award was made under Canada's War Victims Compensation Act, which provides compensation to families of victims of terrorism. The recipient was a Canadian citizen, not a foreign terrorist, and the award was for the death of a Canadian soldier, not an American soldier as falsely claimed in the meme. The meme misrepresents the event to vilify Justin Trudeau.",
